---
description: Testing expectations when changing logic, calculations, or bug fixes
globs: "**/*.test.*, **/*.spec.*, **/tests/**, **/__tests__/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Testing expectations

- Prefer tests that assert observable behavior over implementation details.
- For calculations, money, scoring, validation, and bug fixes: write a failing test first when practical.
- Cover meaningful failure paths, not only the happy path.
- Do not delete, skip, or loosen assertions to make a change pass — explain and ask first.
- Name tests after the behavior under protection so failures are actionable.
